From 54a8ffeb7fc0261c1a88a691debacf37eee99677 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 02:31:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] contract: tq3 is the first family we must renumber, so write
 down why before anyone ports it

tq3 numbers TQ3_4S at 46 and our 46 is TQ4_1S. Both are serialized weight types, so
adopting the originator's id - the rule this document has enforced everywhere else - is
arithmetically unavailable for the first time. tq3's family is remapped to 48+ and its
files need a retag. 47 is skipped for the same reason 44 is.

The mismatch that saves us is a size mismatch: tq3's block is 16 B/32, ours is 20 B/32,
so a tq3 file read as TQ4_1S gets a row size 25% too large and dies at load. That is luck.
Had the blocks matched it would be silent corruption.

Measured, not assumed: all 67 GGUF headers under models/ were scanned, and exactly one
file carries a tq3 id - the YTan Qwen3.8-27B, 504 tensors at 46. The scanner plants a
type-46 tensor and confirms it surfaces, so the number comes from a scan that can fire.

RESERVED and nothing more. The codec is not ported and this commit does not pretend it
is: TQ3_4S is a rotated-domain format at ~496 lines, and rotated-domain dequant is only
correct when a coherence run says so. The note says to land the codec and its proof
before the retag tool, because a retag tool without a working dequant turns a loud load
failure into silent garbage.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5
